{"id": "UgytbQVbDvX1YpdCDoZ4AaABAg", "parent": null, "likes": 0, "text": "❤ I don’t know how many people see this, but I’m fighting Sacoma Cancer for the second time. First time I beat it and beat all the odds, but I know have to fight it again and my fight will be a lot harder. Sarcoma cancer is so aggressive. it killed my little sister in 2014. This Cancer is highly related to NF which runs in my family. I’ll fight to stay alive to my last breath, I have a wife and a beautiful daughter. Since 2009 I had 27 surgeries find this day. Alive has just become a normal day for me. I have a team of eight different doctors working with me in the neurosurgery unit all the way to specialist in the Cancer unit. I just got out of the hospital after spending five days in there they told me my odds of survival are very low. I know you guys don’t know me, but please say a prayer not only for me but for my wife and child. I love Jesus with all of my heart and one day we will all be called home, just us sooner.", "published": "2026-10-16T10:46:33", "replies": 0, "creator": false}
